scoped browser evidence. Ordinary Solo Next prepares the destination while retaining completed results, and starts directly on readiness. Retry preserves complete accepted picture/story identity. Cancellation, failure and stale work preserve the prior result and foreground intent. Historical observations do not establish these journeys on the final deployed source.\n\nExact game source: `fc2c7af6b22c703cc3bb2c081579878b7510f667` (tree `bf11a670ac53a31d58b79540650229160bacd486`).\n\nAll six source gates passed through the hosted exact-source workflow. Each of the two complete four-shard families passed 5,707 tests with zero failures, cancellations, skips or TODOs. Production reproduction/readiness and the ordinary build passed on the hosted source. Both hosted source families used Node 20.19.6. No local command gates are claimed by this qualification pipeline; earlier local P07 cohorts remain separately source-scoped corroboration. The full test suite and ordinary build use the actual hosted authority above; no duplicate local execution is claimed.\n\nThe separately authenticated hosted utility inspected the complete frozen original artifact. Its source archive matches all 10,074 tracked files and modes. Every one of the 690 game files matches its original manifest. Local assembly rehashes the retained original metadata and preserves exact runner member descriptors for the source and distribution payloads; it does not download or rehash the large originals locally. The attached evidence preserves the selected original qualification and source-scoped Solo result continuation observations, including retained earlier failures; it does not replace verification of this release after deployment.\n\nPredecessor: [v0.60.9](https://github.com/mekhovov/revealline/releases/tag/v0.60.9). Before selecting or deploying v0.61.0 as current, preserve its immediate predecessor v0.60.9 as exact immutable published source/distribution/metadata in a capacity-admitted archive, and retain every earlier catalog entry and owner. The ordered v0.60.7, v0.60.8 and v0.60.9 publications, their predecessor retention admissions, and their public acceptance are separate records; this source qualification does not infer them. Bind actual repository/main/tree/run/deployment/status, original receipt inventory, full public byte reconciliation and scoped browser/root admission when those exist. No archive IDs, future assets or accepted state are invented here. Complete the normal main publisher PR/merge, deployed byte verification and applicable native play/offline evidence. Source and attachment qualification alone do not establish public P07 acceptance.\n\nAt package assembly, public byte/play/offline verification is pending; acceptance is recorded separately after publication. Full P03/P05/P07/P18 remains incomplete. Modeled input, browser observations and physical-device qualification remain separate evidence categories.\n"}